{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3431","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3431","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3431\",\"parent_revision\":\"f6fa70fa3e33a93896e2601386bfc4c0eb5932267d94501927e9b4773092aebc\",\"root_revision\":\"f6fa70fa3e33a93896e2601386bfc4c0eb5932267d94501927e9b4773092aebc\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P0\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe active-task record that correlates a stopping sub-agent to its SAM task is keyed by session id. Every sub-agent of one parent session carries the SAME session id, so a plan dispatching N tasks in parallel writes N records to ONE key. Last writer wins; the rest are destroyed silently.\\n\\nREPRODUCTION\\n\\nMeasured on a live session with 13 sub-agents:\\n\\n    $ cat ~/.claude/projects/<project>/<parent-session>/subagents/*.jsonl \\\\\\n        | jq -r 'select(.sessionId).sessionId' | sort -u | wc -l\\n    1\\n    $ ... | jq -r 'select(.agentId).agentId' | sort -u | wc -l\\n    13\\n\\nOne distinct sessionId (the parent's). Thirteen distinct agentId values, one per sub-agent, matching each transcript's filename stem.\\n\\nRecovered from an older parent session 6f9bda8e-f753-41d5-b802-50ab4fbe196a: four sub-agents each ran `active-task set` for a different task (Pe6bcc5c2/T1, /T2, /T3, P8d8ee6f4/T1) and all four passed the same --session-id. The surviving record holds only P8d8ee6f4/T1. The other three registrations were lost.\\n\\nThe context directory holds 27 accumulated records in five incompatible key shapes: 8 parent-session UUIDs (the collision sites), one literal unexpanded ${CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID}, one _default, 15 hand-invented names, 2 bridge-namespace ids.\\n\\nIMPACT\\n\\nTask state can be written to the WRONG task, because the hook resolves a stopping agent to whichever registration last won the shared key. This became more consequential once the SubagentStop matcher was widened off task-worker and the hook began writing BLOCKED: a mis-attributed stop now changes another task's state instead of doing nothing.\\n\\nTask tracking currently survives only via the hook's third fallback, which extracts the task reference from the agent's dispatch prompt. The primary mechanism does not work for parallel dispatch at all.\\n\\nThis is documented harness behaviour, not a Claude Code defect. Codex states it directly: \\\"session_id ... Current Codex session id. Subagent hooks use the parent session id.\\\" (https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks, accessed 2026-09-06). CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID is documented as set in Bash tool subprocesses and as matching the hook JSON session_id, so inside a sub-agent it resolves to the parent's id \u2014 it expanded correctly and still collided.\\n\\nRECOVERABILITY REQUIREMENT\\n\\nAny replacement key must let a new or compacted orchestrator session answer \\\"what is in flight for plan P?\\\" without knowing anything the harness minted at dispatch time. That rules out keying by agent id alone: it is unique but opaque, known only to the hook at stop time, and leaves both directory inspection and record reaping impossible \u2014 the same failure as today's UUID keys.\\n\\nUser-provided context: the hook input carries `agent_id`, documented as \\\"Unique identifier for the subagent. Present only when the hook fires inside a subagent call.\\\", and `agent_transcript_path` already carries that id in its filename. The hook currently opens that file and parses its contents for the non-unique sessionId while the unique identifier sits in the path it was handed. A candidate shape that satisfies both uniqueness and recoverability is to key the record by plan-id + task-id and carry agent_id as a field inside it, so the orchestrator addresses records by what the plan already tells it and only the hook consumes the ephemeral id. Grooming should weigh that against alternatives; an architecture review is in progress.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session audit of task_status_hook.py, 2026-09-06\\n- **Priority**: P0\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a190b2e8e49f29a325852b2cd5bb759ffd01b353c118d13b09cb7d18755f91b1\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABTSBGmQ\"}"}